# Prism: design system instructions

> Read this file before creating or modifying any UI. Follow it exactly. If something is missing, propose an addition instead of improvising.

## 1. Design principles
- **Clarity first.** Give content room to breathe.
- **Consistency over novelty.** Reuse existing components and tokens before inventing anything.
- **Personality:** professional, premium, modern.
- **Accessible by default.** Every color pair, target size and focus state meets the baseline below.
- **Explainable decisions.** Use semantic tokens so every style choice has a stated purpose.

## 2. Color foundations
- Brand: `#06B9A8` (scale 50–950: `--color-brand-50` … `--color-brand-950`); primary actions use an accessible shade of the brand hue.
- Accent: `#F13028`
- Neutral: cool tint, steps 0–1000.
- Status hues: success, warning, danger, info (50–950 each).
- Never use raw primitives in components; consume semantic colors.

